          "id": "12381522",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=becke%40u.washington.edu",
            "name": "becke@u.washington.edu",
            "key": "becke@u.washington.edu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael Becke",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Wow Oleg!  Nice work.  This is quite a thorough addition.  I read it mostly for content and it looks quite \ngood.  There were a few minor grammatical problems which we can fix once it's checked in. \n\nThe only error I noticed was a typo in the ProtocolException section where HttpException was \naccidentally used at the beginning of the paragraph. \n\nContent-wise the only part that stuck out to me was the inclusion of the many exceptions that users \nwill never see.  It's nice that they're documented, but being that it's a user guide I think it may confuse \npeople.  If we could separate the non-user exceptions somehow that would be good.  A separate \nsection may be enough.\n\nMike",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=becke%40u.washington.edu",
            "name": "becke@u.washington.edu",
            "key": "becke@u.washington.edu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael Becke",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2004-07-20T09:40:28.000+0000",
          "updated": "2004-07-20T09:40:28.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333883/comment/12381523",
          "id": "12381523",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=olegk",
            "name": "olegk",
            "key": "olegk",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Oleg Kalnichevski",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "Mike,\nI am glad that several week of self-inflicted misery seem to have resulted in\nsomething useful. I think it now would make more sense if you took it over from\nme. Feel free to rearrange things to your liking and make corrections that you\ndeem necessary. \n\nMeanwhile I concentrate on drafting up the remaining documentation\n\nDo you think that would be OK with you?\n\nOleg",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=olegk",
            "name": "olegk",
            "key": "olegk",
